==> prompt-v1/00-overview.md <==
These prompts change the ONCE Go CLI/TUI in this repository, one feature per file, run in order with a fresh agent for each.

House style here is the project's own Go conventions plus `make lint`; the wider reference copy is at /home/mrjohn/Work/tries/2026-11-03-house-style/house-style

The done line in every file means `make test` and `make lint` both run clean.

==> prompt-v1/01-logs-command.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a `once logs <host>` command here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Logs already stream inside the TUI through the existing log streamer; reuse that so the command follows the app container, supports `--tail` and `--grep`, and exits cleanly on ctrl+c.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/02-status-command.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a `once status <host>` command here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

The app already knows its URL, image, running state, uptime, resource limits and last update and backup results; show all of it in a readable block. A `--json` flag should emit the same data for scripts.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/03-restart-command.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a `once restart <host>` command here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Start and stop already exist and neither pulls an image; restart should stop the current container and start it again without redeploying.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/04-backups-command.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a `once backups <host>` command here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Backups are already written into the configured directory as timestamped archives; list them newest first with date, age and size, and make an empty result obvious.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/05-dashboard-filter.md <==
Your job is to go in and add filtering to the dashboard here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Pressing `/` should open a query field that narrows the panels to matching hostnames or app names as you type; esc clears it and restores every panel. Selection, scrolling and mouse clicks must keep working while the list is filtered.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/06-dashboard-lifecycle-shortcuts.md <==
Your job is to go in and add quick lifecycle keys to the dashboard here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

`x` should toggle the selected app between running and stopped, and `r` should restart it, both using the same progress treatment as the actions menu. The actions menu already has start and stop, so this is only a faster path to them.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/07-update-all.md <==
Your job is to go in and add an Update all action to the dashboard here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

For each app it should check for a newer image and redeploy only when there is one, naming the app currently being updated in the progress line. The per-app update path already exists and must be reused.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/08-health-checks.md <==
Your job is to go in and add continuous HTTP health checks to the dashboard here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Probe each running app's `/up` endpoint on a short interval and show status plus latency on its panel, keeping the last latency visible when an app stops without pretending it is healthy. Deploy-time verification already exists; this is the ongoing version.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/09-app-details.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a full-screen app details view here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Enter on the selected dashboard panel should open it with the URL, image, uptime, resource limits, last update and backup, and a short health and latency history. Esc returns to the dashboard, which already handles selection and overlays.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/10-backup-restore.md <==
Your job is to go in and add restoring from a chosen backup to the backups settings screen here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

List the archives in the configured directory newest first, and let one be selected and restored after a confirmation. The existing restore path creates a new app and refuses a host that is already in use, so this must restore over the selected app in place: stop it, replace its data, run the post-restore hook and redeploy.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/11-logs-stderr.md <==
Your job is to go in and colour stderr differently in the logs screen here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

The log buffer already records whether each line came from stderr; use that to make failures stand out without changing stdout lines.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/12-logs-pause.md <==
Your job is to go in and add pause and resume to the logs screen here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

`p` should freeze the view while lines keep arriving in the background, with a clear paused indicator and a jump to the newest line when resumed.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/13-appearance-settings.md <==
Your job is to go in and add an Appearance settings screen here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

Offer light, dark and auto themes plus a reduced-motion toggle, persist the choice across runs and apply it immediately. Terminal colour detection and the reduced-motion environment variable already exist; this makes them user-facing.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/14-command-palette.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a command palette to the TUI here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

`ctrl+p` should open a searchable list of the actions available on the current screen and run the chosen one exactly as its key would. The menus, key bindings and navigation messages already exist; this is another way into them.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/15-toasts.md <==
Your job is to go in and add transient notifications to the TUI here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

When a start, stop, restart, update, backup or restore finishes, show a short success or failure message that fades after a few seconds without taking focus from the current screen.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

==> prompt-v1/16-chart-time-range.md <==
Your job is to go in and add a time-range selector to the dashboard charts here to this Go CLI/TUI app.

`t` should cycle one minute, five minutes and fifteen minutes, and the CPU, memory and traffic charts plus their peak labels should all follow it. The scrapers already keep ring buffers; grow them enough for fifteen minutes.

Done is when make test runs clean and so do house-style lints

